  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{自動詞|じどうし}→自動詞：10977_jidoushi⟧ (intransitive). No pair verb. Pattern: X⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{泣|な}く (X cries).\n\nASPECT: て⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ indicates ongoing action. {泣|な}いて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ = 'is crying.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {泣|な}いて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ (is crying)\n- {泣|な}かないで (don't cry)\n- {泣|な}き⟦{出|だ}す→出す：01087_dasu⟧ (burst into tears)\n- ⟦{嬉|うれ}し{泣|な}き→嬉し泣き：19040_ureshinaki⟧ (tears of joy)\n\nUSAGE: {泣|な}く describes the act of crying itself; ⟦{涙|なみだ}→涙：02235_namida⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{出|で}る→出る：00513_deru⟧ ('tears come out') focuses on the tears and can happen without any sobbing. The potential form {泣|な}ける is used idiomatically of things, not people: ⟦この→この：00962_kono⟧⟦{映画|えいが}→映画：02273_eiga⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧{泣|な}ける = 'this movie is a tear-jerker.'\n\nKanji {泣|な}く contains the water radical (sanzui), a hint at its meaning. Different from ⟦{鳴|な}く→鳴く：04388_naku⟧ (animal sounds) - homophones with different kanji.",
